Contraindications   U.S. boxed warning: Patients with impaired renal function and those receiving large
and warnings        doses or prolonged therapy have an increased risk for nephrotoxicity and ototoxicity (i.e.,
                    vestibular and auditory), of which ototoxicity may be irreversible.(2) The risk of toxicity can
                    also be increased by elevations in serum concentrations; concurrent use of medications
                    known to be nephro-, neuro-, or oto-toxic; dehydration; and advancing age.(2) Observe
                    closely for signs or symptoms of toxicity.(2) (See Rare Adverse Effects and Monitoring in
                    the Comments section.)
