cautions

Dosage              Although use has been questioned in pediatric patients, the following equation is recom-
                    mended in adult obese patients receiving aminoglycosides.(7-10)
                                   Dosing weight = IBW + 0.4 (TBW – IBW). (See Appendix B.)
                    Loading dose: Aminoglycoside loading doses have been advocated.(2,11-14) Limited data
                    are available, but some advocate an initial amikacin dose of 10–17 mg/kg in neonates
                    and infants.(14)
                    Neonates: Many studies using various dosing methods for aminoglycosides (mostly studied
                    with gentamicin) have been reported in neonates. Most reports have based recommen-
                    dations on weight and postnatal age (PNA)(15-21) or gestational age.(22-37) Use of dose and
                    interval equations based on area-under-the-curve (AUC) has also been recommended in
                    the preterm neonate.(38,39) Although very few studies have been conducted using high-dose
                    extended-interval amikacin in premature neonates, traditional dosing (7.5 mg/kg/dose)
                    has become less commonly recommended with large dose, extended-interval regimens
                    becoming accepted practice. PNA, at which any of these aminoglycoside regimens are
                    applicable, has not been well studied, but the few studies delineating a PNA have gener-
                    ally been ≤7 days of age.(18,22,24-27,28,31,34,38)
