                 vivo recovery (IVR) should be measured and baseline plasma vWF:RCo and FVIII:C should
                 be assessed in all patients prior to surgery. The IVR is calculated by measuring baseline
                 plasma vWF:RCo; then infuse vWF/RCo 60 international units/kg IV at time zero; mea-
                 sure vWF:RCo at 30 minutes after infusion. The IVR = (plasma vWF:RCo at 30 minutes
                 minus plasma vWF:RCo at baseline) divided by 60 international units/kg. A standardized
                 loading dose may be used when individual IVR is not available; based on assumed IVR
                 of 2 international units/dL for every 1 vWF:RCo international unit/kg administered.(3,5,9)
