                 bleeding in Hemophilia A and vWD, usually 2–3 times weekly. Dose should be individualized
                 based on age, venous access, activity and availability of clotting factor concentrates.(10-13)
                 In a recent study, 17 children and adolescents as well as 12 adults with vWD (types 1–3)
                 received Humate P or Wilate at a median dose of 40 international units/kg based on
                 vWF:RCo activity baseline and 24-hour trough levels. Patients received infusions between
