Preparation and         Allow product to come to room temperature before reconstitution. Use transfer needle
delivery                provided or syringe and needle to transfer diluent into vial of drug. Gently agitate or
                        rotate vial after addition of diluent. Do not vigorously shake vial. Do not refrigerate after
                        reconstitution, administer within 3 hours after reconstitution.(1-4) Use plastic syringes;
                        proteins may adhere more to glass syringes.(2-4)
                        Humate-P was found to be stable for 14 days at room temperature after reconstitution
                        per manufacturer directions in a study by Lubetsky.(13) Mean vWF:RCo assay was 64.3 ±
                        4.9 international units/mL following reconstitution and 53 ± 7 international units/mL at
                        day 14 in the presence or absence of heparin (4 units/mL of factor concentrate).(14)


IV push                 Alphanate should be administered at a maximum rate of 10 mL/min.(2)
                        Humate P should be administered at a maximum rate of 4 mL/min.(3)
                        Wilate should be administered at a maximum rate of 2–4 mL/min.(4)


Intermittent infusion   No information


Continuous infusion     Continuous infusion has been used in the treatment of moderate and severe bleeds in
                        hemophilia as well as in limited studies in vWD. It has been shown that using a continu-
                        ous infusion of factor after initial homeostasis is achieved can result in less overall factor
                        consumption by avoiding the peaks and troughs associated with bolus dosing.(14-19)
                        Humate-P was reconstituted and administered via minipump with added heparin (4 units/
                        mL of factor concentrate) in 8 patients with mild-to-severe vWD. Initial bolus dose and
                        rate of infusion were determined by pharmacokinetic evaluation and adjusted to maintain
                        vWF:RCo levels of 0.5–0.7 international units/mL during the first days of treatment. Rate
                        of infusion was adjusted daily per ristocetin cofactor clearance. Treatment with continu-
                        ous Humate-P was effective in stopping bleeding episodes or preventing bleeding during
                        or after surgical interventions.(14)


