Brand names         ATryn, Thrombate III


Medication error    None noted; however, products are not interchangeable. Use caution with dosing and
potential           product selection.(1,2)


Contraindications   Contraindications: None known for Thrombate III.(1) For ATryn, hypersensitivity to goat
and warnings        and goat milk proteins.(2)
                    Warnings
                        Thrombate III(1): Because it is made from human plasma, there is a risk of trans-
                        mitting infectious agents, though no cases have been identified.
                        The anticoagulant effect of heparin is enhanced by concurrent treatment with Throm-
                        bate III in patients with hereditary antithrombin III (ATIII) deficiency; reduced dosage
                        of heparin is recommended during treatment with Thrombate III.
                        ATryn(2): Anaphylaxis and severe hypersensitivity reactions are possible.
                        The anticoagulant effect of drugs that use antithrombin to exert their effect may
                        be altered during use with ATryn; regularly monitor anticoagulants during and after
                        withdrawal of ATryn therapy and monitor patients for bleeding or thrombosis.


Infusion-related    None noted for Thrombate III. Infusion of entire dose in 10–20 minutes is generally well
cautions            tolerated.(1) For ATryn, monitor closely for signs of allergic-type hypersensitivity (hives,
                    generalized urticaria, chest tightness, wheezing, hypotension, and anaphylaxis). If these
                    occur, treatment must be discontinued, and emergency treatment must be administered.(2)


Dosage              Both commercially available antithrombin products only have approved labeling for adults
                    with hereditary antithrombin deficiency, and manufacturers state that safety and effec-
                    tiveness in pediatric patients have not been established.(1,2)
                    Dosing equations
                        Eq. 1: (Thrombate III)(1) Antithrombin III units required: [desired % – baseline %
                        ATIII level] × weight (kg)/1.4
                        Eq. 2a: (ATryn)(2) Antithrombin III loading dose (units) for surgical patients: [100 –
                        baseline % ATIII level] × weight (kg)/2.3
                        Eq. 2b: (ATryn)(2) Antithrombin III maintenance infusion (units/hr) for surgical patients:
                        [100 – baseline % ATIII level] × weight (kg)/10.2
                        Eq. 3a: (ATryn)(2) Antithrombin III loading dose (units) for pregnant patients: [100 –
                        baseline % ATIII level] × weight (kg)/1.3
                        Eq. 3b: (ATryn)(2) Antithrombin III maintenance infusion (units/hr) for pregnant
                        patients: [100 – baseline % ATIII level] × weight (kg)/5.4
                    Hereditary antithrombin deficiency (in conjunction with surgical procedure(1,2)
                    or to treat thromboembolism(1))
                        Using Thrombate III: Dose calculated using equation 1 targeting normal ATIII
                        activity (80% to 120%). Repeat doses determined based on response to first dose
                        (see Monitoring, Thrombate III in the Comments section).(1)
                        Using ATryn: Dose calculated using equations 2 (a and b) or 3 (a and b). Check
                        ATIII activity once or twice per day and adjust (see Monitoring, ATryn in the Com-
                        ments section).(2)




