Antithrombin III
Dosage (cont.)          Veno-occlusive disease (VOD): In 48 patients (age 1–68 years, median 39 years) with
                        VOD (Baltimore criteria), ATIII (Thrombate III) was given targeting ATIII activity levels
                        of 120% (equation 1). Target ATIII activity levels were achieved in only 37% of patients,
                        but 83% of patients were alive at day 100.(13) In a study (91 patients [0.2–19 years old])
                        aimed at giving ATIII supplementation as prophylaxis against VOD (modified Seattle
                        criteria) in stem cell transplant recipients after busulfan-based conditioning regimens,
                        ATIII supplementation failed to prevent VOD. Dosing strategy in this study: Three times
                        weekly ATIII activity levels with preemptive supplementation if <70% using a product
                        not available in the United States (Kybermin) at 50–100 units/kg, repeated until ATIII
                        activity level 100%.(14)


Dosage adjustment       Specific recommendations for dosage adjustment are not included in manufacturer
in organ dysfunction    labeling.(1,2)


Maximum dosage          Some studies reported giving whole vials to minimize waste (e.g., 1000 units of an anti-
                        thrombin product not available in the United States), which equaled 283 units/kg at the
                        highest (patients ≤20 kg on ECMO)(7) or up to 295 units/kg using Thrombate III (patients
                        1 day to 19.5 years old on ECMO).(8) Highest reported dose of ATryn was 520 units/kg/
                        day (patients 4 days to 3 years old on ECMO).(5)


Additives               Thrombate III is prepared from pooled units of human plasma and contains not more than
                        0.1 unit of heparin per unit of ATIII. It is preservative-free and contains sodium 110–210
                        mEq/L after reconstitution with SWFI.(1)
                        ATryn is not formulated with human plasma proteins and contains no heparin. It is
                        preservative-free. Each vial of 525 international units package strength contains 30 mg
                        glycine, 23.7 mg sodium chloride, and 7.8 mg sodium citrate. Each vial of 1750 inter-
                        national units package strength contains 100 mg glycine, 79 mg sodium chloride, and
                        26 mg sodium citrate.(2)


