                                                                                                    Antithrombin III
Comments                            Monitoring
                                         Thrombate III manufacturer recommends obtaining ATIII level at baseline and
                                         20 minutes postinfusion of first dose; subsequent doses should be based on the
                                         response achieved from the first dose. Afterward, check ATIII levels at least q 12 hr
                                         and before the next dose to maintain ATIII level >80%. These guidelines can be
                                         modified for individual patients.(1)
                                         ATryn manufacturer recommends checking ATIII activity level once or twice per day,
                                         starting at 2 hours after initial dose) and adjusting dose as follows(2):
                                              ATIII activity level <80%: Increase dose 30% and recheck ATIII 2 hours later.
                                              ATIII activity level 80% to 120%: No change to current dose. Recheck ATIII
                                              6 hours after initiation of treatment or dose adjustment.
                                              ATIII activity level >120%: Decrease dose 30% and recheck ATIII 2 hours later.
                                              Surgery or delivery may rapidly decrease ATIII activity; check ATIII level just
                                              afterward and give additional bolus (loading) dose if needed.(2)
                                         Monitoring during therapy for ECMO or other uses (off-label): Follow institu-
                                         tional protocols. Tests used to monitor the efficacy and safety of anticoagulation may
                                         include some or all of the following: ACT, aPTT, anti-Xa (for UFH or low molecular
                                         weight heparin [LMWH] as appropriate), ATIII activity, and TEG, in conjunction with
                                         coagulation factor levels, CBC, fibrin deposition in the circuit, and other signs of clot-
                                         ting or bleeding in the circuit or the patient.(3-8)
                                    Pharmacokinetic considerations: Molecular weight of antithrombin is reported as
                                    approximately 57,000–58,000 daltons.(1,2)
                                    Drug interactions: The anticoagulant effect of UFH and LMWH is enhanced by antithrom-
                                    bin. The half-life of antithrombin may be altered by concomitant treatment with UFH or
                                    LMWH due to consumption or altered turnover; thus, monitoring of anticoagulant effect
                                    is imperative.(1,2)


