                    tion with good muscle recovery times.(6) Authors of an opinion-based review on dosing
                    adjustments of anesthetic agents in morbidly obese patients recommend atracurium
                    be dosed using ideal body weight to avoid prolonged duration of paralysis.(36) Pediatric
                    consensus guidelines also recommend using ideal body weight for atracurium dosing.(17)
                    Dosing adjustment for hypothermic cardiac bypass: Smaller atracurium doses (50%
                    of usual infusion) may be required in patients undergoing hypothermia (25°C to 28°C)
                    during cardiac bypass.(2)
                    Dosing adjustment during concomitant inhaled anesthetic agents: Atracurium
                    infusions should be reduced by 33% in patients undergoing enflurane or isoflurane anes-
                    thesia; a smaller dose reduction is required for halothane anesthesia.(2)
