                        min) has been used in those >1 month of age and 0.4 mg/kg/hr (6.7 mcg/kg/min) has
                        been given to neonates.(11)
                        Occasionally, continuous infusion doses as large as 2.4 mg/kg/hr (40 mcg/kg/min) may
                        be required.(14) In one study, seven pediatric patients required a mean infusion of 1.72
                        mg/kg/hr (28.7 mcg/kg/min) for up to 72 hours.(20) A case report described a 17-year-old
                        who received 4.5 mg/kg/hr (75 mcg/kg/min) but experienced prolonged muscle weakness
                        afterward.(23) (See Significant Adverse Effects in the Comments section.)


