delivery                before use. Refer to appropriate reference for more information on compatibility with other
                        drugs and solutions, compatibility following Y-site delivery, and suggested storage and
                        extended stability.(24)
                        Atracurium is an acidic solution; do not administer with alkaline solutions.(2,24)
                        May be incompatible with propofol; however, the potential for incompatibility is concen-
                        tration dependent and formulation specific.(24)


IV push                 10 mg/mL given rapidly or over 1 minute in patients with a history of histamine reactions.(2)


Intermittent infusion   No information is available to support administration by this method.(2,3,7)


Continuous infusion     0.2–0.5 mg/mL(2,24)


