potential


Contraindications      Contraindications: In patients with known hypersensitivity to aztreonam or any other
and warnings           component in the formulation.(1)
                       Warnings: Although the manufacturer recommends caution when aztreonam is given
                       to patients with immediate hypersensitivity reactions to penicillins or cephalosporins,(1)
                       the cross-reactivity between cephalosporins and penicillins does not appear to extend to
                       the monobactams. Patients with penicillin hypersensitivity have been given aztreonam
                       without incident.(2-5,20) Similarly, those who experience hypersensitivity to aztreonam may
                       not be hypersensitive to other beta-lactam antibiotics.(6)
                       Prolonged use may cause superinfection and/or Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea
                       (CDAD), which has been reported and may range in severity from mild diarrhea to fatal
                       colitis.(1)


