Comments                           Drug interactions: IV calcium should be used cautiously in patients receiving cardiac
                                   glycosides because of the potential for development of arrhythmias.(2)
                                   Adverse effects: Bradycardia, hypotension, and cardiac arrhythmias may occur.(2)
                                   Calcinosis cutis occurred in an 11-year-old boy within 3 weeks of calcium gluconate infu-
                                   sion.(26) Extravasation of calcium gluconate in a premature neonate resulted in calcinosis
                                   cutis and compartment syndrome.(27)
                                   Osmolarity: 10% calcium gluconate solution is 0.68 mOsmol/mL (680 mOsmol/L).(2)
                                   Other: Calcium gluconate bioavailability is considered to be less than that of calcium
                                   chloride. In 49 critically ill children aged 1 day to 17 years who received equivalent doses
                                   of either calcium chloride or calcium gluconate (0.136 mEq/kg) for hypocalcemia, ion-
                                   ized calcium concentrations were increased 30 minutes after the infusion in both groups;
                                   however, patients who received calcium chloride had greater increases in ionized calcium
                                   compared to those who received calcium gluconate.(28) In 10 stable burn patients aged
                                   13 months to 17 years who received equivalent infusions of calcium chloride and calcium
                                   gluconate (0.035 mEq/kg) in a crossover study, ionized calcium concentrations were not
                                   different 10 minutes after infusion.(29)
                                   Calcium gluconate is the preferred calcium salt in parenteral nutrition due to better solu-
                                   bility. When compounding parenteral nutrition solutions, phosphorus is recommended to
                                   be added first and calcium added at the end of mixing.(25)



