                       mcg/kg/min.(9) In another study including 19 infants and children receiving cisatracurium,
                       the maximum infusion rate was 10 mcg/kg/min.(10) Response may vary over time, result-
                       ing in the need for dosage adjustment.(2) Patients with burns may develop resistance to
                       nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocking agents.(2) The extent of resistance is affected by
                       the size of the burn and time since the burn injury.


