                    NovoSeven, its components, or who have hypersensitivity reactions to mouse, hamster, or
                    bovine proteins.(1) Use caution when administering rFVIIa to patients with increased risk of
                    thromboembolic complications, such as liver disease, sepsis, crush injury, coronary heart dis-
                    ease, disseminated intravascular coagulation, postoperative immobilization and neonates.(1)
                    Factor VII deficient patients should be monitored for the formation of antibodies. If the
