Dosage                 Consult individual protocols for complete dosing information.
                       Cyclophosphamide is used as a component of combination therapy to treat both oncologic
                       and nononcologic diseases. Specifically, the FDA approves it for the oncologic treatment
                       of lymphomas, Hodgkin disease, multiple myeloma, leukemias, mycosis fungoides, neu-
                       roblastoma, ovarian adenocarcinoma, retinoblastoma, and breast cancer.(3) Nononcologic
                       FDA indications include pediatric minimal change nephrotic syndrome.(3) It may also be
                       used in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), rheumatoid arthritis, vasculitis, autoimmune
                       hemolytic anemia, idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura, antibody-induced pure red cell
                       aplasia, and in consolidation therapy prior to autologous bone marrow transplant (BMT).
                       Selected dosage regimens include the following:
                       Pediatric malignancy
                           Induction: 40–50 mg/kg IV (1.5–1.8 g/m2) in divided doses over 2–5 days(3)
                           Maintenance: 10–15 mg/kg (350–550 mg/m2) given q 7–10 days or 3–5 mg/kg
                           (110–185 mg/m2) twice weekly(3,5)
                       SLE: 500–750 mg/m2 every month (maximum dose 1 g/m2).(5,6) Continuous daily doses
                       of 60–120 mg/m2 (1–2.5 mg/kg) have been given every day.(6,7)
                       HSCT-conditioning regimen: 50 mg/kg IV once daily for 3–4 days, starting 5 days prior
                       to transplant.(4,7,8) May also use 60 mg/kg/day for 2 days after busulfan.(8)


Dosage adjustment      If CrCl is <10 mL/min, administer 75% of the usual dosage.(3,9)
in organ dysfunction
                       Hemodialysis: Administer 50% of normal dose after dialysis session.(9)
                       Continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis (CAPD): Administer 75% of normal dose.(9)
                       Continuous renal replacement therapy (CRRT): Administer 100% of normal dose.(4,9)


