                    Warnings: Myopathy and rhabdomyolysis have been reported with daptomycin use.
                    Patients should be monitored for muscle pain and weakness. Creatine phosphokinase
                    (CPK) should be monitored at least weekly and more frequently in patients receiving
                    concomitant HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors, who have renal impairment, or who have had
                    an increased CPK with daptomycin therapy. CPK elevations may occur more frequently
                    when dosed more than once per day.(3)
                    Hypersensitivity reactions have been reported. If allergic reactions occur daptomycin
                    should be stopped and appropriate measures taken.(3)
                    Eosinophilic pneumonia has been reported 2–4 weeks after starting daptomycin therapy. If
                    this occurs daptomycin should be stopped and systemic steroid therapy is recommended.(3)
                    Daptomycin use may cause superinfection and/or Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea
                    (CDAD), and may range in severity from mild diarrhea to fatal colitis. If CDAD is suspected
                    or confirmed, appropriate fluid and electrolyte management, protein supplementation,
                    antibiotic treatment of C. difficile, and surgical evaluation should be instituted as clini-
                    cally indicated.(3)


