                    impaired left ventricular systolic function, reduced contractility, and congestive heart failure,
                    and death. Cardiotoxicity is dose-dependent and may occur months or years after therapy
                    is completed. The incidence increases after a total cumulative dose exceeding 300 mg/m2
                    in children >2 years, or 10 mg/kg in children <2 years. Clinicians should monitor for total
                    cumulative dose and patients should be monitored long-term.(3)
