                                        Dexamethasone Sodium Phosphate
Comments (cont.)                    Recommendations published in 2003 designed to improve neonatal outcomes suggested
                                    avoiding dexamethasone in the first 10 days of life.(58) For patients requiring dexametha-
                                    sone, recommendations were 0.2–0.3 mg/kg/day divided q 12 hr for 48 hours, and if
                                    treatment was extended beyond 48 hours, the dose should be halved q 48 hr with a
                                    maximum treatment length of 10 days.(58) The updated AAP Policy Statement published in
                                    2010 recommends against high-dose regimens (0.5 mg/kg/day) and suggests that low-
                                    dose regimens (<0.2 mg/kg/day) may facilitate extubation with fewer adverse outcomes;
                                    however, it finds insufficient evidence to make a recommendation. Studies evaluating
                                    low-dose regimens have been encouraged.(4)
                                    DART investigators conducted a randomized, multicenter, controlled trial of low-dose
                                    dexamethasone (initial dose 0.15 mg/kg/day and tapering over 10 days) in 70 extremely
                                    low birth weight infants after the first week of life. Dexamethasone facilitated extubation,
                                    shortened duration of mechanical ventilation, and did not cause any short-term adverse
                                    effects.(5) Two small trials evaluating even lower dosing regimens have also been published.
                                    In 16 extremely premature babies who had failed extubation attempts, a 9-day tapering
                                    regimen starting with 0.05 mg/kg/day (cumulative 0.24 mg/kg) appears to successfully
                                    facilitate extubation.(6) A retrospective matched study comparing low-dose dexametha-
                                    sone to placebo in 76 ventilator-dependent babies <30 weeks gestational age or <1500 g
                                    finds dexamethasone 0.05 mg/kg/day for 10 days followed by alternate-day doses for
                                    6 days (cumulative 0.65 mg/kg) superior to placebo for improving respiratory function
                                    and extubation rates, with no increase in hypertension, hyperglycemia, or GI perforation/
                                    hemorrhage.(7) Reversible hypertrophic cardiomyopathy has been reported in two babies
                                    who received very-low-dose (0.05 mg/kg/day) dexamethasone.(69)
                                    Adverse effects: Musculoskeletal effects, fluid and electrolyte abnormalities, cataracts,
                                    and hyperglycemia.(64) Patients with diabetes may be at particular risk for hyperglycemia.
                                    Drug interactions: Drugs that enhance hepatic clearance (e.g., phenytoin, phenobarbital,
                                    carbamazepine, and rifampin) may decrease blood levels and lessen physiologic activity.
                                    Drugs that inhibit hepatic clearance may increase dexamethasone concentrations.(64,41)
                                    Dexamethasone may decrease the serum concentration of caspofungin, possibly necessitat-
                                    ing increased dosing for caspofungin.(41) Steroids may potentiate neuromuscular blockade;
                                    monitor patients receiving concomitant nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocking agents.(41)
                                    Live virus vaccines may be given 1 month after ending a ≥2-week course of high-dose
                                    systemic corticosteroids (2 mg/kg/day of prednisone or its equivalent, or 20 mg/day if
                                    >10 kg).(59)


