administration

Comments                            Monitoring: Monitor for signs and symptoms of an acute allergic reaction (e.g., urticaria,
                                    pruritus, erythema, angioedema, bronchospasm with wheezing or cough, stridor, laryn-
                                    geal edema, hypotension, tachycardia) and treat immediately with appropriate emer-
                                    gency medical care (e.g., oxygen, diphenhydramine, corticosteroids, volume expansion
                                    and airway management). If anaphylactoid reaction occurs discontinue the DigiFab and
                                    administer epinephrine.(2)
                                    Clinical improvement in signs and symptoms of digitalis toxicity generally occur within
                                    ≤30 minutes of DigiFab administration.(2) Complete reversal of cardiac and noncardiac
                                    manifestations generally occur 3–4 hours after completion of the infusion.(11) The diagnosis
                                    of digitalis toxicity should be questioned if the patient fails to respond to an adequate
                                    dose of DigiFab.
                                    Serum potassium should be monitored closely as concentrations may fall rapidly (i.e., within
                                    30 minutes) after initiation of DigiFab. Continue to monitor for several hours after admin-
                                    istration.(2,9) ECG should be monitored for evidence of conduction disturbances.(2)
                                    Laboratory interference: DigiFab in human serum interferes with many radioimmu-
                                    noassays for digoxin to produce a significant overestimation of concentration.(4,12-15) This
                                    interference precludes the use of total serum digoxin concentrations in patients treated with
                                    digoxin immune Fab. To determine the degree of interference, review the manufacturer
                                    specification for the assay used at your institution. If a patient is in need of readministra-
                                    tion of DigiFab due to recurrent toxicity or to a new toxic episode that occurs soon after
                                    the first episode, measurement of free (unbound) serum digitalis concentrations should
                                    be considered since DigiFab may still be present in the body.
                                    Other: Digoxin should not be initiated until Fab fragments have been eliminated from the
                                    body.(2-4) This may take several days in those with normal renal function and may take
                                    more than a week in patients with impaired renal function.(2-4)


