Comments                Rare adverse effects: Cases of acute myocardial infarction and arrhythmias have
                        occurred in adults.(1) One report noted intestinal ischemia in a 4-year-old after a total of
                        8 doses of 0.1 mg q 8 hr.(5)
                        Drug interactions: The concurrent administration of potent CYP3A4 inhibitors with
                        dihydroergotamine should be avoided.(1) Examples of potent CYP3A4 inhibitors include
                        antifungals (e.g., ketoconazole and itraconazole), the protease inhibitors (e.g., ritonavir,
                        nelfinavir, and indinavir), and macrolide antibiotics (e.g., erythromycin, clarithromycin,
                        and troleandomycin). Other less potent inhibitors (e.g., saquinavir, nefazodone, fluco-
                        nazole, grapefruit juice, fluoxetine, fluvoxamine, zileuton, and clotrimazole) should be
                        administered with caution.(1) These lists are not exhaustive; therefore, consult appropriate
                        resources before combining any drug with dihydroergotamine mesylate.
