                        ergotamine to reduce the incidence of abdominal discomfort.(1) Concomitant antiemetics
                        may not be needed with IM administration.(8) One study used prochlorperazine or meto-
                        clopramide 30 minutes prior to dihydroergotamine for the first 3 doses and then used
                        ondansetron PRN for subsequent doses to decrease risk of extrapyramidal side effects
                        noted with repeated exposure to antidopaminergic drugs.(4)




