Preparation and                      Preparation: Vials are reconstituted with 10 mL SW or NS. Suspension must be further
delivery                             diluted with NS or D5W.(2,11)
                                     Stability: After dilution with NS, may be stored up to 72 hours under refrigeration or
                                     12 hours at room temperature and when diluted with D5W up to 24 hours under refrig-
                                     eration or 4 hours at room temperature.(2)


IV push                              Not recommended


Intermittent infusion                Administer over 1 hour.(2,11) Extended 4-hour infusions have been used.(9,10,12,18)


Continuous infusion                  Not administered by this method


Other routes of                      None
administration

Comments                             Rare adverse effects: Although seizures are reported with carbapenem use, it appears
                                     less frequent with doripenem.(13-15)
                                     Drug interactions: Doripenem reduces serum concentrations of valproic acid. (2,16)
                                     ­Probenecid decreases doripenem clearance.(2)


