administration

Comments                Rare adverse effects: Angioedema generally occurs after the first dose but may also
                        present at any time during therapy.(3) Edema may occur in the head, neck, extremities,
                        or intestines; angioedema of the larynx, glottis, or tongue may cause airway obstruction
                        that constitutes a medical emergency.(3)
                        The risk of anaphylactoid reactions with high-flux dialysis and plasmapheresis (lower risk)
                        with concurrent ACE-inhibitor therapy.(18)
                        Cholestatic jaundice has occurred and may progress to fulminant hepatic necrosis that
                        can prove fatal.(3)
                        Maternal exposure: Infants with a history of in utero exposure to an ACE inhibitor
                        should be observed for hypotension, oliguria, and hyperkalemia. If oliguria occurs, it is
                        important to support blood pressure and enhance renal perfusion. Exchange transfusion
                        or dialysis may be required.(3)
                        Monitoring: In addition to blood pressure and signs of angioedema, monitor serum cre-
                        atinine/urine output, WBC (i.e., neutropenia, agranulocytosis), and potassium. Transient
                        hyperkalemia (>5.7 mEq/L) was reported in about 1% of hypertensive adults in clinical
                        trials.(3) In most cases hyperkalemia resolved despite continued therapy.
                        Pharmacokinetics: Neonates have decreased elimination and extended duration of
                        action; hence, they may experience prolonged hypotension and acute renal failure.(6,10)
                        Drug interactions: A number of clinically significant drug interactions have been reported.
                        Consult appropriate resources for dosing recommendations before combining any drug
                        with enalaprilat.



