Dosage (cont.)              Children on chemotherapy ≥5 years and adolescents: 600 units/kg IV once
                            weekly until completion of chemotherapy(2)
                            After 4 weeks, if Hb remains <10 g/dL and has not increased by >1 g/dL, increase
                            dose to 900 units/kg. Maximum dose 60,000 units/dose. Discontinue after 8 weeks
                            if no hemoglobin response or if RBC transfusions are still needed.(2)
                            Anemia of prematurity: 100–400 units/kg IV or sub-Q either 2–3 times a week
                            up to 10 weeks,(8,9-11) 250 units/kg IV or sub-Q 3 times weekly, or 300 units/kg IV or
                            sub-Q 5 times a week for 2 weeks(12)
                            Epidermolysis bullosa: 150–350 units/kg 3 times a week(13)
                        Preoperative surgery (to reduce the need for blood transfusion): In cardiac surgery,
                        150 or 300 units/kg given 2–3 times approximately 1 week prior to surgery and postop-
                        eratively for 2 doses or until the hematocrit is increased to the preoperative value.(14,15)


Dosage adjustment       No dosage adjustment is required.(2)
in organ dysfunction

