Continuous infusion     Can be mixed in IV fluids containing at least 0.05% protein (amino acids).(18)


Other routes of         The sub-Q route is preferred except in patients on hemodialysis when IV administration
administration          is preferred.(2,4) For sub-Q administration, the dose can be diluted 1:1 with bacteriostatic
                        0.9% sodium chloride injection, USP, with benzyl alcohol 0.9%. The benzyl alcohol in the
                        bacteriostatic saline decreases the discomfort from sub-Q injection. This is not neces-
                        sary when using the multidose product that contains benzyl alcohol.(2) (See the Additives
