Contraindications      Contraindications: In patients with a known hypersensitivity to any component of this
and warnings           product or to other carbapenems or in patients who have demonstrated anaphylactic
                       reactions to beta-lactams.(3)
                       Warnings
                           Allergic reactions: Serious hypersensitivity and occasionally fatal anaphylactic
                           reactions have been reported.(3) These are more likely in patients who are sensitive
                           to multiple allergens and in those with a history of penicillin, cephalosporin, or other
                           beta-lactam hypersensitivity.(3,4)
                           Seizures: Neurotoxicity with the carbapenem antibiotics has been reported.(3) Seizures
                           occur most commonly in patients with renal impairment and/or underlying neurologic
                           disorders. (See the Comments section.)
                           Superinfection: Ertapenem use may cause superinfection and/or Clostridium difficile-
                           associated diarrhea (CDAD), which has been reported and may range in severity from
                           mild diarrhea to fatal colitis.(3) If CDAD is suspected or confirmed, appropriate fluid and
                           electrolyte management, protein supplementation, antibiotic treatment of C. difficile,
                           and surgical evaluation should be instituted as clinically indicated.(3) Discontinuation
                           of antibiotics not directed against C. difficile should be considered.(3)


Infusion-related       Serious anaphylactic reactions require immediate emergency treatment.(3)
cautions

Dosage                 Not for use in meningitis due to decreased CNS penetration(3)
                       3 months to 12 years: 30 mg/kg/day divided q 12 hr up to 1 g/day(3,6,7,9,16)
                       13–17 years of age: 1 g/day.(3,6,7,8) Duration of therapy varies depending on the type
                       and severity of infection, as well as causative organism.


Dosage adjustment      If CrCl is ≤30 mL/min, a dose decrease of 50% is recommended in adults.(3)
in organ dysfunction

Maximum dosage         1 g/day(3)


Additives              Contains approximately 137 mg (6 mEq) of sodium/g of ertapenem.(3,10)


Suitable diluents      NS(3,10)


Maximum                20 mg/mL(3,10)
concentration

Preparation and        Stability: Immediately dilute reconstituted solution in NS.(3,10) Diluted solution can
delivery               be stored at room temperature (25°C) and used within 6 hours or may be stored for
                       24 hours under refrigeration (5°C).(3,10) Should be used within 4 hours after removal from
                       refrigeration.(3,10)
                       Compatibility: Do not dilute in dextrose containing solutions.(3,10)


IV push                Not administered by this method




