                                                                                                                         Ertapenem
Intermittent infusion                Over 30 minutes(3,10)


Continuous infusion                  Not administered by this method


Other routes of                      May be administered IM following reconstitution with 1% lidocaine HCl injection, USP (in
administration                       saline without epinephrine).(3,10,11) Maximum duration of IM therapy is 7 days.(3)


Comments                             Rare adverse effects: Neurotoxicity of the carbapenem antibiotics has been reported.(12,13)
                                     Seizures appear to be related to an underlying CNS disorder, impaired renal function, and/
                                     or large doses.(3,13) Because of the risk of seizures, carbapenems should be used cautiously
                                     in patients with renal dysfunction, patients with history of seizure disorders, and when
                                     used in combination with drugs that lower the seizure threshold.(3,14) If seizures occur, the
                                     need for ertapenem should be considered and the dosage should be assessed.(3)
                                     Drug interactions: Oral probenecid may increase serum concentrations of ertapenem.(3)
                                     Carbapenems may reduce serum concentrations of valproic acid, which can result in a loss
                                     of seizure control.(3,15) Serum valproic acid concentrations should be monitored frequently
                                     after beginning or increasing the dose of a carbapenem. Alternative antibiotics should be
                                     considered for patients controlled on valproic acid.(3)
                                     Other: Although there is a theorectical allergic cross-reactivity of carbapenems with
                                     penicillins and cephalosporins, studies have found this to be very rare.(17,18)


