Maximum                           0.8 mg/mL(2)
concentration

Preparation and                   Delivery: No other medications should be given through the same IV site or tubing
delivery                          as esomeprazole. The IV line should be flushed with D5W, NS, or LR, before and after
                                  esomeprazole administration.(2)
                                  Stability: The manufacturer states that esomeprazole sodium is stable in either NS or
                                  LR for 12 hours and is stable in D5W for 6 hours.(2) Another study has found solutions
                                  of esomeprazole 0.4 and 0.8 mg/mL to be physically and chemically stable in D5W, LR,
                                  and NS for a minimum of 2 days at room temperature and 5 days refrigerated. Samples
                                  stored at room temperature and refrigerated samples reconstituted with D5W developed a
                                  yellow tint within 24 hours; this discoloration was associated with <10% loss of activity.(9)


IV push                           0.4–0.8 mg/mL over at least 3 minutes(2)


Intermittent infusion             Dilute reconstituted drug (0.4 mg/mL or 0.8 mg/mL) to a total volume of 50 mL with
                                  suitable diluent and infuse over 10–30 minutes.(2)


