                       0.4 mg/kg up to 25 mg sub-Q twice weekly or 0.8 mg/kg sub-Q up to 50 mg once a
                       week. If given twice weekly, doses should be separated by 72–96 hours. Children weighing
                       <31 kg should be dosed from the multidose vial and not a prefilled syringe. Those weighing
                       ≥63 kg may use the 50-mg prefilled syringe.(2,5,6)
                       Psoriasis in children 4–17 years: 0.4 mg/kg sub-Q twice weekly or 0.8 mg/kg (up to
                       50 mg) once a week. If given twice weekly, doses should be separated by 72–96 hours.(7-9)
                       Chronic uveitis: 0.4 mg/kg up to 25 mg sub-Q twice weekly. Infliximab may be more
                       effective in preventing uveitis than etanercept.(10-13) (See the Comments section.)


