                    AlphaNine SD and Mononine are prepared from human pooled plasma and may carry a risk
                    for transmission of infectious agents, despite viral attenuation processes.(2,3,5,7) Hepatitis
                    A and B vaccination are recommended in all hemophilia patients.(7)
                    Serious and potentially fatal thrombosis or disseminated intravascular coagulation may
                    occur in patients with hepatic impairment and in patients undergoing surgery. Use with
                    caution in patients with liver disease, neonates, postoperatively, or patients with signs of
                    fibrinolysis. Monitor all patients closely for thromboembolic complications.(2-4,6)
