                       kg/min) was the most effective dose; no effect on blood pressure <0.2 mcg/kg/min while
                       larger doses (>1–1.2 mcg/kg/min) produced no additional benefit in decreasing blood
                       pressure; heart rate was significantly elevated at 3.2 mcg/kg/min.(3)
                       Diuresis during/after cardiopulmonary bypass (neonates and infants):
                       0.05–0.3 mcg/kg/min titrated over 24 hours to a maximum dose of 1 mcg/kg/min has
                       been given for 1–15 days in neonates unresponsive to conventional diuretic therapy;
                       urine output (UOP) increased from 3.6 to 5.8 mL/kg/hr.(4) Another study found a reduction
                       in diuretic and vasodilator use when 1 mcg/kg/min was administered to infants during
                       bypass.(5) Conversely, 0.1 mcg/kg/min during surgery and continued for 72 hours was found
                       to have no effect on UOP, fluid balance, or acute kidney injury incidence in neonates.(6)
                       Diuresis or to enhance renal perfusion in critically ill patients (0–18 years): A
                       retrospective study of 13 patients receiving 0.01–0.5 mcg/kg/min observed increased UOP
                       without unfavorable adverse effects in the 24-hour period after initiating fenoldopam.(7)
                       Severe hypertension (children 1–17 years): 0.2–0.8 mcg/kg/min.(8) Slow titration
                       (0.05–0.1 mcg/kg/min q 15 min) and lower initial doses (0.03–0.1 mcg/kg/min) results
                       in less reflex tachycardia in adults.(1)
                       Prevention of acute kidney injury: 0.2 mcg/kg/min titrated up to 0.4 and 1.5 mcg/
                       kg/min has been reported in two children with severe cardiomyopathy and acute kidney
                       injury on ventricular assist devices; in one patient (8 years old), UOP increased, BUN and
                       SCr decreased, and renal replacement therapy was avoided on 0.4 mcg/kg/min (duration
