                                    and can cause unexpected hypotension; if possible, avoid concomitant use.(1)
                                    Monitoring: Blood pressure and heart rate should be monitored continuously, preferably
                                    intra-arterially. Serum electrolytes should be monitored; hypokalemia has been observed.(1)
                                    Other: One neonate receiving fenoldopam for 48 hours after Norwood procedure acutely
                                    clotted the Blalock-Taussig shunt and required extracorporeal membrane oxygenation
                                    therapy for resuscitation; this event was thought to be potentially related to the brisk
                                    diuresis achieved.(4)
