Contraindications       Contraindications: Hypersensitivity to ferric gluconate or its components(1)
and warnings

Infusion-related        Although serious hypersensitivity reactions, some fatal, have been reported(1) they have
cautions                been at a much lower rate with ferric gluconate than with iron dextran products.(2-6,14)
                        Typical reactions during infusions include flushing, hypotension, nausea, vomiting, and
                        diarrhea,(2,3,6) which may be related to release of free iron. Premedication may not decrease
                        the incidence of reactions.(7)


Dosage                  An erythropoiesis stimulating agent should be used concurrently.
                        Iron deficiency in hemodialysis (chronic renal failure): 1.5 mg/kg (≤125 mg/dose)
                        elemental iron × eight dialysis sessions is recommended.(1,8,9) Doses of 1–5 mg/kg have
                        been evaluated and doses >3 mg/kg have shown limited additional efficacy and potential
                        for added toxicity.(11)


Dosage adjustment       No information is available.
in organ dysfunction

Maximum dosage          Although doses >3 mg/kg have been used, they may be associated with increased adverse
                        effects.(11,12) Maximum total dose is 125 mg.(1)


Additives               Contains 9 mg benzyl alcohol/mL.(1) (See Appendix C for more specific information about
                        benzyl alcohol toxicity in neonates.)


Suitable diluents       NS.(1) Stability in other solutions has not been evaluated and is not recommended.(1)


Maximum                 12.5 mg/mL(1)
concentration

Preparation and         Dilution in dextrose is not recommended.(1)
delivery

IV push                 Up to 12.5 mg/min in adults.(1) Higher infusion rates may be associated with increased
                        adverse effects.(12)


Intermittent infusion   Over 1 hour per dialysis session(1)


Continuous infusion     Not indicated(1)


Other routes of         Not indicated(1)
administration




