                    vestibular and auditory), of which ototoxicity may be irreversible.(3) The risk of toxicity
                    can also be increased by prolonged elevations in serum concentrations, concurrent use
                    of medications known to be nephro-, neuro-, or oto-toxic, dehydration, and advancing
                    age.(3) Observe closely for signs or symptoms of toxicity.(3) (See Rare Adverse Effects,
                    Monitoring, and Drug Interactions in the Comments section.)
