                    have revealed that morbidly obese patients (BMI ≥40 kg/m2) required lower infusion rates
                    based on actual body weight compared to nonobese patients,(10) and that higher prophylaxis
                    dosing of sub-Q heparin or enoxaparin (heparin dosing: 7500 units TID compared to 5000
                    units BID or TID) was associated with lower odds of VTE without an increase in bleeding
                    risk.(50) Another study in adults suggested using a calculated dosing weight based on either
                    of the following two equations, where DW = dosing weight, IBW = ideal body weight, and
                    ABW = actual body weight(51):
                        DW = IBW + 0.3 (ABW – IBW), or
