in organ dysfunction   is necessary. If CrCl is <10 mL/min, administer 75% of the normal dose.(9)
                       Hemodialysis: Administer 1000 mg/m2 followed by hemodialysis 6–8 hours later.(9)
                       Continuous renal replacement therapy (CRRT): No dosage adjustment is needed.(9)
                       No specific guidelines exist on ifosfamide use in patients with hepatic insufficiency. However,
                       one investigator recommended a decrease in the ifosfamide dosage by 75% in patients
                       with an aspartate aminotransferase >300 units/L or a bilirubin >3 mg/dL.(10)

