administration

Comments                             Rare adverse effects: Cochlear and/or vestibular ototoxicity has been associated with
                                     all aminoglycoside antibiotics.(1) Either total dose (>500 mg/kg)(12) or total AUC are better
                                     indicators of ototoxic risk than either peak or trough.(22,23)
                                     Aminoglycosides may accumulate leading to oliguric renal failure. This has been associated
                                     with elevated trough serum concentrations. Risk of nephrotoxicity may increase if
                                     aminoglycosides are combined with other potentially nephrotoxic drugs.(1) Use with caution
                                     with other drugs known to cause ototoxicity.
                                     Monitoring: Because large variability exists in patient response to therapy, individualize
                                     dosage based on serum concentrations, clinical response, and renal function. Although
                                     serum concentration monitoring has become routine practice in many institutions, not all
                                     patients receiving aminoglycosides require monitoring.(24,25)
                                     Laboratory interference: Serum concentrations may be falsely elevated when samples
                                     are collected through central venous silastic catheters.(26) Concomitant use with cephalo-
                                     sporins may falsely elevate creatinine.(1)


