                        continuous infusion ranging from 36–410 mg/24 hr. She received long-term therapy for
                        67 days in a homecare setting.(29)

Other routes of         IM.(2,16,17,30,31) Laryngospasm was more common with IM compared to IV ketamine.(31)
administration
                        Caudally administered ketamine (in addition to local anesthetic) has been used to reduce
                        analgesic requirements in patients undergoing urological, lower abdominal, or lower limb
                        surgery.(32) Has been given intraosseously in adults.(37)

Comments                Adverse effects
                            Emergence reactions: Dream-like states, hallucinations, and/or delirium may occur
                            up to 24 hours after surgery. Frequency is less in pediatric patients than in adults.(2)
                            The incidence may be decreased when patients are premedicated with a benzodi-
                            azepine. When premedicated with midazolam prior to ketamine, 1% of those <10
                            years of age and 4.2% of those ≥10 years of age experienced a severe emergence
                            reaction.(8) Minimizing verbal, tactile, and visual stimulation after dosing decreases
                            the likelihood of these reactions.(2) Short- or ultra-short acting barbiturates may be
                            used as treatment.(2)




