                       cardiogenic shock, uncompensated congestive heart failure, severe bradycardia, heart
                       block (except in patients with a functioning artificial pacemaker); in conditions associated
                       with severe and prolonged hypotension.(3)
                       Caution in patients with hyper-reactive airway disease or bronchospastic disease, dia-
                       betes mellitus, compensated heart failure, hepatic impairment, peripheral vascular
                       disease and Raynaud disease, history of psychiatric illness, myasthenia gravis, and
                       pheochromocytoma.(3)
