Lacosamide Injection
Comments (cont.)                          Cardiovascular: Lacosamide enhances slow inactivation of voltage-gated sodium chan-
                                          nels and may produce a dose-related increase in the PR interval or cause AV block.(1,15,16)
                                          Cardiac problems are more likely to occur in patients with known conduction problems,
                                          patients with severe disease (e.g., heart failure), or those receiving medications known
                                          to prolong the PR interval (e.g., beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers).(1)
                                          Suicidal behavior/ideation: The risk of this adverse effect has been noted to be
                                          greater than placebo (0.43% versus 0.24% risk) in patients receiving anticonvulsants
                                          as either monotherapy or as adjuvant therapy for the treatment of epilepsy, psychi-
                                          atric disorders, and other conditions. The FDA requires that the product labeling of
                                          the entire class of antiepileptics include a warning concerning the risk of suicide.(1)
                                          Other: IV loading doses of 400 mg in adults were associated with dizziness, somno-
                                          lence, and nausea.(17) Angioedema has been noted in adults following 2 doses of IV
                                          lacosamide and later in the course of therapy.(4) Lacosamide may worsens seizures
                                          in those with LGS.(18)
                                     Monitoring: ECG should be closely monitored before and after initiation of lacosamide
                                     in any patient with known conduction problems, severe heart disease, or those receiving
                                     medications known to prolong the PR interval.(1)
                                     Drug interactions: Consult appropriate references before combining any drug with
                                     lacosamine as it clearance many be affected by drugs that impact CYP3A4, CYP2C9, and
                                     CYP2C19.(1)


