Brand names            Carnitor, generic


Medication error       Look-alike, sound-alike drug names. LevOCARNitine has been confused with levETIRAce-
potential              tam, but patient harm did not occur.(1)


Contraindications      None known
and warnings

Infusion-related       None known
cautions

Dosage                 Hemodialysis: 10–40 mg/kg/dose following dialysis.(2-4) Others support the use of smaller
                       doses of 2–5 mg/kg/dose following dialysis.(5-7) Clinical practice recommendations in chil-
                       dren with chronic kidney disease states there is no firm evidence to support the use of
                       levocarnitine for anemia.(8)
                       Primary carnitine deficiency/metabolic disorders: A loading dose of 50 mg/kg fol-
                       lowed by 50–60 mg/kg/day divided q 3–6 hr or given by continuous IV infusion(2,9)
                       PN supplementation in neonates/infants with little or no enteral intake: 10–30
                       mg/kg/day(10-18)
                       Valproate-associated hepatotoxicity
                           Active hepatotoxicity/overdose: 150–500 mg/kg/day, up to 3 g/day(19,20)
                           Prophylaxis against valproate or other anticonvulsant-associated hepato-
                           toxicity: 15–100 mg/kg/day has been used in children with or without hyperammo-
                           nemia.(20) Decreased ammonia levels, in those with hepatotoxicity, were seen after
                           9 days of treatment with 1000 mg/m2/day divided in 2 equal doses.(21)
                       Other uses: See the Comments section.


Dosage adjustment      No dose adjustment recommended(2); however, carnitine is excreted renally and renal
in organ dysfunction   insufficiency may lead to the accumulation of potentially toxic metabolites.(8)


Maximum dosage         PN supplementation: 48 mg/kg/day has been given.(22) (See the Comments section.)
                       Metabolic disorders: 300 mg/kg/dose (age not specified)(2)
                       Valproate-induced hepatotoxicity: 3 g/day(19,20)
                       Valproic acid (VPA)/anticonvulsant therapy: 100 mg/kg/day or 1000 mg/m2/day(20)


Additives              None reported


Suitable diluents      NS, LR(2)


