Brand names            Synthroid, generic


Medication error       ISMP reports that levothyroxine has been confused with lamotrigine, liothyronine, and
potential              Lanoxin.(1)


Contraindications      U.S. boxed warning: Should not be used for weight loss or the treatment of obesity.
and warnings           Large doses of levothyroxine may produce serious and life-threatening toxicity, particularly
                       when given in combination with sympathomimetic agents.(3)
                       Other warnings: Recommend cautious initiation of therapy in patients with cardiovascular
                       disease and endocrine disorders.(3)


Infusion-related       Excessive bolus doses of IV levothyroxine may have cardiovascular risks.(3)
cautions

Dosage                 Congenital hypothyroidism: The AAP and the European Society for Paediatric Endocri-
                       nology recommend an initial oral dosage of 10–15 mcg/kg/day for infants with hypothy-
                       roidism.(7,13) Oral bioavailability is estimated to be 48% to 74% in adults(3); therefore, the
                       IV dose should be no more than 80% of the oral dose.(13) Adjust dosage based on clinical
                       response and serum free T4 and TSH.(3,7,13)
                       The goal of therapy is to normalize T4 within 2 weeks and TSH within 1 month.(7) Neonates
                       and infants with very low or undetectable serum T4 concentrations (<5 mcg/dL) should
                       be started at the higher end of the dosage range.(5,6) Patients with evidence of cardiac
                       disease should receive a lower starting dose.(3)
                       Acquired hypothyroidism
                       The following has been recommended in older infants and children(5):
                        Age                      Oral Doses Listed Below (IV doses should
                                                 be based on the oral bioavailability, which is
                                                 estimated to be 48% to 74%.(3))
                        6–12 mo                  5–8 mcg/kg/day(5)
                        1–3 yr                   4–6 mcg/kg/day(5)
                        3–10 yr                  3–5 mcg/kg/day(5)
                        10–18 yr                 2–4 mcg/kg/day(5)


Dosage adjustment      No information is available.
in organ dysfunction

Maximum dosage         Not established. In adults with myxedema coma or stupor, without concomitant severe
                       heart disease, may give doses of 300–500 mcg.(3)


Additives              Contains mannitol.(3,9)


Suitable diluents      Use only NS for reconstitution.(3,9)


Maximum                100 mcg/mL(9)
concentration

Preparation and        Preparation: Reconstitute with NS only. Use immediately.(3)
delivery




