Dosage adjustment       No adjustment in renal impairment.(3,22) 10 mg/kg q 12 hr is recommended for all ages
in organ dysfunction    receiving intermittent hemo- or peritoneal dialysis.(22) Although metabolites may accumu-
                        late in renal insufficiency, the clinical significance is unknown.(3) No adjustment in mild-
                        to-moderate hepatic impairment; although pharmacokinetics have not been studied.(3)

Maximum dosage          45 mg/kg/day divided q 8 hr has been reported in a 7-week-old infant.(18) 1200 mg/day
                        if >12 years of age.(3,4)

Additives               100 mL contains 1.7 mEq sodium, 200 mL contains 3.3 mEq of sodium, and 300 mL
                        contains 5 mEq of sodium.(3,23)

Suitable diluents       Compatible with D5W, NS, and LR.(3,23) May be given undiluted.(23)

