Comments                             Significant adverse effects: If the WBC count is between 2000–3000/mm3 or if platelet
                                     levels are between 50,000–75,000/mm3, the dose should be decreased by half. The drug
                                     may be stopped if the WBC count is <2000/mm3 or platelet levels are <50,000/mm3.(1)
                                     Patients are at an increased risk for infectious complications. The use of anti-infective
                                     prophylaxis is recommended.(1)
                                     Monitoring: Measurement of T-cell counts helps assess T-cell depletion.(1) The WBC count
                                     and platelet levels should be monitored during therapy.(1)


