IV push                           Not recommended(3)


Intermittent infusion             To avoid a paradoxical pressor effect, dilute in 50–100 mL D5W (≤10 mg/mL) and infuse
                                  slowly over 30–60 minutes.(4,10)


Continuous infusion               No information is available to support administration by this method.


Other routes of                   IM and sub-Q administration are not recommended due to erratic absorption.(10)
administration

Comments                          Significant adverse effects: May cause hemolysis in patients with glucose-6-phosphate
                                  dehydrogenase deficiency.(2) May cause positive Coombs test; if evidence of hemolytic
                                  anemia, the drug should be discontinued.(2)
                                  Monitoring: CBC at baseline and periodically during therapy; Coombs test at baseline
                                  and at 6 and 12 months of therapy; liver function tests at baseline over the first 6–12
                                  weeks of therapy; and any time there is unexplained fever.(2)
                                  Other: May cause urine to be discolored (pink/red to darkened).(2)
                                  A paradoxical pressor response has been reported.(4)


