administration

Comments                           Significant adverse effects: Adverse effects most commonly occurring in one pediatric
                                   study were elevations in serum transaminases and alkaline phosphatase, hyperbilirubi-
                                   nemia, and nausea.(16)
                                   Arrhythmias and hypotension have been reported in adults.(4)
                                   Drug interactions: Micafungin is a poor substrate for the CYP3A4 isoenzyme and is
                                   associated with the potential for drug interactions. Concomitant administration of mica-
                                   fungin may cause sirolimus, itraconazole, or nifedipine toxicity, and dosage of sirolimus,
                                   itraconazole, or nifedipine should be reduced, if necessary. Consult appropriate resources
                                   for dosing recommendations before combining any drug with micafungin.(3,16)
                                   Pharmacokinetic considerations: One neonatal study compared three dosing regimens
                                   (0.75, 1.5, and 3 mg/kg/day) in two infant weight groups (500–1000 g and >1000 g).
                                   Infants <1000 g only received 0.75 mg/kg/dose. The smaller infants had decreased serum
                                   concentrations and increased clearance when compared to the larger infants.(20)


