                                                                  Morphine Sulfate
Dosage (cont.)   Additional regimens published: Premedication for nonemergent intubation,
                 0.05–0.1 mg/kg IV/IM once.(10) (See Other in the Comments section.)
                 Intermittent dosing: 0.05 mg/kg IV, IM or sub-Q q 4–6 hr (max 0.1 mg/kg/dose);
                 continuous infusion of 0.001–0.03 mg/kg/hr.(12-19) Based on achieving a therapeutic mor-
                 phine concentration of 15 ng/mL, an infusion of 0.0075 mg/kg/hr would be appropriate
                 at term birth and 0.0125 mg/kg/hr at 1 month of age.(20,21) Of note, a decreased
                 gestational age and postconceptional age are directly related to clearance.(15,16,18,19)
                 (See the Comments section.)
                 Infants/children: WHO Guidelines recommend the following as starting doses in
                 opioid-naive patients, based on age.(43)
                     Intermittent (IV/sub-Q)
                         1–6 mo: 0.1 mg/kg q 6 hr
                         6–12 mo: 0.1 mg/kg q 4 hr
                         1–2 years: 0.1 mg/kg q 4 hr up to maximum 2.5 mg/dose (as initial dose)
