                            >20 kg: 5 mg/day for 10–14 days
                        Cardiac or BMT transplant rejection: 0.1–0.2 mg/kg/day (maximum ≤5 mg) for
                        7–14 days.(10-12)
                        CD3+ cell counts should be <25/mm3 and OKT3 serum concentration ≥800 ng/mL
                        in children.(1,2)
                    Acute viral myocarditis: Five children (15 months to 16 years of age) with left ven-
                    tricular ejection fractions of 5% to 20% were treated with a variable combination of
                    corticosteroids, cyclosporine, azathioprine, IV immunoglobulin, and OKT3 dosed at 0.1
                    mg/kg/day for 10–14 days.(13)




