Contraindications      Contraindications: Hypersensitivity to oxacillin or other penicillins or any component
and warnings           of the formulation.(2)
                       Warnings: Individuals who have a type I reaction to penicillin may experience serious
                       and occasionally fatal hypersensitivity (anaphylactic shock with collapse) reactions.(2)
                       (See Appendix C for specific information.)
                       Oxacillin use may cause superinfection and/or Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea
                       (CDAD), which has been reported and may range in severity from mild diarrhea to fatal
                       colitis.(2) If CDAD is suspected or confirmed, appropriate fluid and electrolyte manage-
                       ment, protein supplementation, antibiotic treatment of C. difficile, and surgical evaluation
                       should be instituted as clinically indicated.(2)


