                           Treatment (those who are intolerant of trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole
                           (TMP/SMX) or who do not respond to TMP/SMX)
                               Infants >5 months, children, and adolescents: 4 mg/kg IV once daily for
                               14–21 days.(1,2,8,9) If there is clinical improvement after 7–10 days, oral atovaquone
                               or trimethoprim/dapsone can be used to complete the treatment.(9)
                               Prophylaxis: Although IV pentamidine has been used, it is no longer recom-
                               mended for PJP prophylaxis.(9) If TMP/SMX is not tolerated, aerosolized pentami-
                               dine 300 mg/dose monthly via the Respirgard II nebulizer can be used in children
                               (usually >5 years of age) who are able to use the device.(2,9) One study evaluated
                               4 mg/kg IV given monthly in pediatric oncology patients intolerant of TMP/SMX.(10)
                               Breakthrough PJP was higher in infants than in older children leading investigators
                               to suggest that other options need to be investigated in infants.(10)
                       Trypanosomiasis treatment (non-CNS involvement): IM, IV 3–4 mg/kg/dose once
                       daily for 21 days(11)

Dosage adjustment      CrCl 10–30 mL/min: Usual dose q 36 hr(13)
in organ dysfunction
                       CrCl <10 mL/min: Usual dose q 48 hr(13)
                       Hemodialysis: Usual dose q 48 hr after dialysis on dialysis days(13)
                       Peritoneal dialysis: Usual dose q 48 hr(13)
                       Continuous renal replacement therapy (CRRT): No adjustment needed(13)
                       Neither the safety nor efficacy of dosage adjustments in renal or hepatic dysfunction is
                       known.(1)

Maximum dosage         4 mg/kg(1)

Additives              None

Suitable diluents      D5W. Reconstitute with SWFI for IM injection and SWFI or D5W for IV injection. Do not
                       use NS to reconstitute because precipitation will occur.(1,14)

