                       mEq/kg/hr.

Dosage adjustment      Potassium is renally eliminated; therefore, extreme caution is required when dosing
in organ dysfunction   patients with renal insufficiency.(3) In six 19- to 37-year-old adults with sickle cell disease
                       and normal glomerular filtration, urinary potassium excretion was significantly less than
                       individuals without sickle cell disease during an infusion of 0.75 mEq/kg over 2 hours.(12)

Maximum dosage         Close monitoring of ECG and serum concentrations is required and all sources of potas-
                       sium should be considered in determining the dose.
                       Dosage requirements are based on serum potassium concentrations. Intermittent infu-
                       sions should not exceed 1 mEq/kg/hr including all sources.
                       Serum potassium >2.5 mEq/L: 10 mEq/hr up to 200 mEq/day in adults(3)
                       Serum potassium <2 mEq/L: 40 mEq/hr up to 400 mEq/day in adults(3)

