cautions            of propofol should be discarded after 12 hours. Collect blood from IV port opposite to
                    the site of propofol infusion or temporarily suspend infusion and flush port prior to blood
                    draw. Transient pain has been noted in 45% of pediatric patients when a small vein of
                    the hand is used without lidocaine pretreatment.(4) This can be reduced to <10% when
                    pretreated with lidocaine (1 mL of a 1% solution; not to exceed 20 mg lidocaine per 200
                    mg propofol) or when the antecubital veins is used.(5) Cardiorespiratory depression has
                    occurred during bolus dosing or after rapid increase in the dosage rate. Assess the patient
                    frequently and wait 3–5 minutes between dosage adjustments.(4) Abrupt discontinuance
                    of propofol should be avoided.(4) (See the Comments section.)

