                        given over 20–30 seconds until onset of induction.(4,6-14) Noncommunicative and non-
                        verbal children with cerebral palsy require less propofol than healthy children.(15) Those
                        >16 years should be given 40 mg (2–2.5 mg/kg) q 10 sec until onset of induction.(4)
                        Those >16 years who have a neurosurgical diagnosis should receive smaller doses
                        (i.e., 20 mg [1–2 mg/kg] q 10 sec).(4)
