Dosage (cont.)          Acute kidney injury with elevated uric acid levels: A single dose of 0.2 mg/kg was
                        administered to a late preterm neonate who had anuria and a serum uric acid level of
                        14 mg/dL. He began to produce urine within 12 hours of the dose and subsequently had
                        serum uric acid levels of 0,5 mg/dL at 48 hours and 2.8 mg/dL 5 days postdose.(16)
                        Hyperuricemia with AKI secondary to rhabdomyolysis caused by ecstasy intoxi-
                        cation and exceptional heat stroke: A single dose of 6 mg (0.086–0.092 mg/kg) was
                        administered to a 15-year-old (uric acid level of 20.2 mg/dL) and an 11-year-old (uric
                        acid level of 13.6 mg/dL) with complete recovery in both patients.(17)
                        Hemolytic uremic syndrome: A 9-month-old infant with diarrhea-associated HUS and
                        uric acid level of 12.3 mg/dL received a single dose of 0.18 mg/kg, and within 12 hours
                        the uric acid had decreased to 0.3 mg/dL. He was discharged on hospital day 7 in good
                        condition, and at 2-month followup his uric acid level was 4.2 mg/dL.(18)


