Additives               Contains 9 mg/mL NaCl and polysorbate 80(4) and trisodium citrate dihydrate 7.35 mg/mL.


Suitable diluents       D5W or NS(4)


Maximum                 4 mg/mL(4)
concentration

Preparation and         Do not mix or dilute with other drugs.(4,22)
delivery

IV push                 Not recommended(4)


Intermittent infusion   Dilute with NS or D5W to final concentration of 1–4 mg/mL and infuse at a beginning
                        rate of 50 mg/hr. If no hypersensitivity reactions occur, the rate may be escalated by
                        50 mg/hr q 30 min to a maximum rate of 400 mg/hr. In patients tolerating the first infu-
                        sion, subsequent cycles may begin at a rate of 100 mg/hr, increase q 30 min by 100
                        mg/hr, escalating up to a maximum rate of 400 mg/hr.(4) If infusion related reactions or
                        hypotension occur, slow or stop infusion. Restart infusion after resolution of symptoms
                        at 50% of the previous rate.


Continuous infusion     No information is available to support administration by this method.


Other routes of         No information is available to support administration by other routes.
administration



