Comments                             Significant drug interactions: Avoid concomitant use with other immunosuppressants
                                     and monoclonal antibodies (e.g. pimecrolimus, abciximab, natalizumab). Avoid use of live
                                     vaccines for at least 3 months after therapy. Therapeutic effects of inactivated vaccines
                                     may be diminished.(4)
                                     Significant adverse effects: Rituximab is associated with a minimal (<10%) risk of
                                     emesis.(21) Generally, prophylaxis for acute and delayed emesis is not needed.
                                     Monitoring: CBC with platelets, liver, cardiac and renal function, and fluid balance. Monitor
                                     vital signs during and after infusion for infusion-related hypersensitivity reaction, including
                                     anaphylaxis, chills, fever, rigors, hypotension, angioedema, bronchospasm and hypoxia.
                                     Severe infusion-related reactions may occur 30–120 minutes after initiation of infusion.
                                     Cardiac monitoring is recommended during and after infusion in patients with preexisting
                                     cardiac disease or if arrhythmias develop during infusion.(4)
                                     Antihypertensive medications should be held for 12 hours prior to infusion.(4)


