SUFentanil Citrate
Comments                             Significant adverse effects: Caution should be used when administering sufentanil to
                                     patients with head trauma. It has been associated with increases in intracranial pressure
                                     in this population.(21)
                                     Pharmacokinetic considerations: The elimination half-life is shorter in infants and
                                     children and longer in neonates compared to that of adolescents and adults.(5,22) Clear-
                                     ance can be further reduced by up to one third in neonates with cardiovascular disease.(5)
                                     Ten male children with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency safely received
                                     sufentanil 0.2 mcg/kg for perioperative analgesia without evidence of hemolysis.(23)
                                     Other: Sufentanil produced EEG changes in preterm neonates resembling sleep states
                                     and burst suppression.(11)


