Brand names            Tygacil


Medication error       None reported
potential

Contraindications      U.S. boxed warning: Although the cause has not been determined, all cause mortality
and warnings           was increased with tigecycline over comparators.(2)
                       Contraindications: In those with known hypersensitivity to tigecycline.(2)
                       Warnings: Tigecycline is a tetracycline derivative and should be administered cautiously
                       in patients with hypersensitivity to tetracycline.(2) Life-threatening anaphylaxis/anaphy-
                       lactoid reactions have occurred.
                       Use of tetracyclines during tooth development (last half of pregnancy, infancy, and
                       childhood to the age of 8 years) may cause permanent tooth discoloration (yellow-gray-
                       brown).(2) Tigecycline should not be used in this age group unless alternative drugs do
                       not exist.(2)
                       Elevation in transaminases, total bilirubin concentration, and prothrombin time have been
                       noted and isolated cases of significant hepatic dysfunction/failure have occurred.(2) Patients
                       who develop abnormal liver function tests should be monitored for worsening function
                       and the risk to benefit of continuing therapy should be assessed.(2)
                       Lower cure rates and higher mortality were seen when patients with ventilator-associated
                       pneumonia were treated with tigecycline.(2)
                       Monotherapy should be avoided in those with complicated intra-abdominal infection
                       secondary to clinically apparent intestinal perforation as sepsis/septic shock has been
                       reported.(2) Although APACHE II scores were different from baseline, the relationship of
                       this outcome to treatment cannot be established.(2)
                       Tigecycline use may cause superinfection and/or Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea
                       (CDAD), which has been reported and may range in severity from mild diarrhea to fatal
                       colitis.(2) If CDAD is suspected or confirmed, appropriate fluid and electrolyte manage-
                       ment, protein supplementation, antibiotic treatment of C. difficile, and surgical evaluation
                       should be instituted as clinically indicated.(2)


Infusion-related       None reported
cautions

Dosage                 Safety and effectiveness in pediatric patients below the age of 18 years have not been
                       established. The manufacturer recommends against use in pediatric patients unless no
                       alternative therapy exists.(2) Due to reports of increased mortality in adults, few pediatric
                       trials have been conducted.(2,11)
                       Children 8–11 years of age: 2.4 mg/kg/day divided q 12 hr(2,4)
                       Children ≥12 years of age: The manufacturer recommends 100 mg/day divided q 12 hr for
                       patients 12–17 years of age.(2) One reference suggests 1.5 mg/kg as a single dose (maximum:
                       100 mg/dose) followed by 2 mg/kg/day (maximum: 50 mg/dose) divided q 12 hr.(5)
                       A loading dose of 3 mg/kg, followed by 6 mg/kg/day divided q 8 hr was successfully used
                       in combination with daptomycin in a 21-month old with Enterococcus faecium meningitis.(6)


Dosage adjustment      No dosage adjustment is necessary in renal impairment or mild-to-moderate hepatic
in organ dysfunction   impairment (Child Pugh A and Child Pugh B).(2) Patients with severe hepatic impairment
                       (Child Pugh C) should be treated with caution. The initial dose should be 100 mg followed
                       by a reduced maintenance dose of 25 mg q 12 hr in adults.(2)


Maximum dosage         Initial dose of 100 mg and 50 mg/dose thereafter(2)




