administration

Comments                           Rare adverse effects: Tigecycline is structurally similar to tetracycline-class antibiotics
                                   and may have similar adverse effects including photosensitivity, pseudotumor cerebri,
                                   and anti-anabolic action (which has led to increased BUN, azotemia, acidosis, and
                                   hyperphosphatemia).(2)
                                   Pancreatitis is a known adverse effect of the tetracyclines and has also been reported with
                                   tigecycline.(2,8,9) There is a case report in a 9-year-old child.(10)
                                   Monitoring: The manufacturer recommends that prothrombin time or other suitable
                                   anticoagulation test should be monitored in those given warfarin.(2) Monitor patients
                                   periodically for abnormal liver function and observe for diarrhea.


