                       VariZIG 125 international units of lypholized powder must be reconstituted using a diluent
                       that contains a total volume of 8.5 mL. However, only 1.25 mL of the diluent is needed for
                       a final volume of 100 units/mL. Consider adding an auxiliary label to remind practitioners
                       about only using 1.25 mL of diluent per vial to achieve 100 units/mL.
                       International units may be confused with IV.
