Vasopressin
Maximum                             1 unit/mL(2)
concentration

Preparation and                     Preparation: Undiluted for sub-Q or IM use(6,30)
delivery
                                    Stability: It is recommended to refrigerate unopened vials. Vials may be stored at
                                    room temperature for up to 12 months or until vial expiration date from manufacturer,
                                    if sooner. Use diluted vasopressin solution within 18 hours at room temperature or 24
                                    hours refrigerated.(2)


IV push                             20 units/mL.(3) See Cardiac Arrest in the Dosage section.


Intermittent infusion               Not indicated


Continuous infusion                 0.1–1 unit/mL(2)


Other routes of                     IM or sub-Q.(6,30) IO(3) (preferred) and ET administration may be used during CPR if unable
administration                      to obtain IV access.(17,21) Intra-arterial infusion may be used for GI hemorrhage.(21)


Comments                            Adverse effects: An increased incidence of hyponatremia has been observed in some
                                    patients.(27,29,32)
                                    Monitoring: Blood pressure, distal pulses, signs of water intoxication (headaches and
                                    drowsiness),(3) and fluid and electrolyte status should be monitored.(27,29,32)
                                    Drug interactions: The antidiuretic and pressor effects of vasopressin may be potenti-
                                    ated when used with drugs suspected of causing SIADH (e.g., SSRIs, TCAs, haloperidol,
                                    enalapril, pentamidine). Conversely, concomitant use of drugs suspected of causing dia-
                                    betes insipidus may antagonize the effects of vasopressin. Osmolar clearance and urine
                                    flow may be increased with concomitant use of furosemide.(2)


