                            1 to 8, 13 to 20, and 25 to 32(22)
                        Wilms Tumor, infant and children: 0.75–1.5 mg/m2/does IV weekly for 10–11 weeks,
                        then every 3 weeks for 15 additional weeks; maximum dose 2 mg. Variable frequency,
                        refer to institutional protocols.(23,24)

Dosage adjustment       Dose should be reduced in patients with hepatic insufficiency.(25) The manufacturer rec-
in organ dysfunction    ommends a 50% decrease in dose if direct serum bilirubin is >3 mg/dL.(4) Other sources
                        recommend a 50% reduction in dose if the serum bilirubin is 1.5–3 mg/dL, or transami-
                        nases are 2–3 times ULN or alkaline phosphatase is increased.(8,36,37) One source recom-
                        mends that if serum bilirubin is >3 mg/dL, vincristine use should be avoided.(36) No dose
                        reduction is needed in patients with renal dysfunction.(26)

Maximum dosage          Most, but not all, clinical trials and treatment protocols have maximum dose guidelines of
                        2 mg in order to minimize neurotoxicity.(27) However, some clinicians have questioned the
                        appropriateness of the 2-mg maximum vincristine dose.(28) Refer to treatment protocols
                        for maximum dose guidelines.
                        In pediatric patients less than 13 years of age, severe toxicity symptoms may occur after
                        doses of 3–4 mg/m2 and death has occurred following doses 10 times the recommended
                        therapy.(4)

Additives               100 mg mannitol(4)

Suitable diluents       D5W, NS(4,5)

Maximum                 1 mg/mL(5)
concentration

Preparation and         Vincristine must be dispensed with a sticker affixed directly to the container which states
delivery                “Fatal if given intrathecally. For IV use only.” Vincristine must also be dispensed in over-
                        wrap that bears the statement “Do not remove covering until the moment of injection.
                        Fatal if given intrathecally. For IV use only.”(4,5)
                        Vincristine injection should be diluted into flexible plastic containers (minibags) prior
                        to administration to reduce potentially fatal errors. Dilute with NS in concentrations of
                        0.0015–0.08 mg/mL.(38) Stable for up to 24 hours if protected from light or 8 hours at
                        25°C under normal light conditions.(4)

IV push                 1 mg/mL administered via an intact, free-flowing IV needle or catheter over 1 minute.(5)

Intermittent infusion   May dilute with suitable diluent and infuse over 4–8 hours.(5)

Continuous infusion     May dilute with suitable diluent and infuse continuously.(5)




