Comments                Significant adverse effects: The most commonly reported adverse effects in children
                        are dose-dependent visual disturbances and increases in transaminases and bilirubin,
                        and photosensitivity.(3)
                        Therapy has been associated with prolongation of QT interval.(2) Serum electrolytes (potas-
                        sium, magnesium, calcium) should be within range before starting therapy to reduce risk
                        of arrhythmias.(2)
                        Stevens-Johnson syndrome has been reported rarely.(2)
